				{
					"type": "MainSpriteFontEmoji1",
					"properties": {
						"text": "[color=8E150B]Alex:[/color]\n\n[color=B4AB90]I notice these almost archetypal, folk characters explode from your pixels! '[color=ffffff]^=[/color]mushroom cloud[color=ffffff]=^[/color]' and '[color=ffffff]$$[/color]The Council[color=ffffff]$$[/color]' have their own unique, deeply affective faces. What draws you to exporting these expressions?[/color]\n\n[color=003DA2]Adelaide:[/color]\n\n[color=B4AB90]I really just go with whatever I think feels right at the time, until some tangible idea or structure reveals itself. A face is arguably the most recognizable figure to exist and, because of my process... or lack thereof, a recurring theme within my paintings.[/color]\n",
